# Create MUI Wrapper Component Workflow

## MUI Wrapper Component Creation Checklist

### 1. File Structure
- **Location**: `src/components/mui/ComponentNameComponent.jsx`
- **Naming**: PascalCase with `Component` suffix
- **Pattern**: Wrap every MUI component the app actually uses (Button, TextField,
  Card, Dialog, …) rather than importing `@mui/material` primitives directly
  all over the codebase — this gives theme-level behavior (loading states,
  consistent `sx` defaults) one place to live.
- **Current state**: `src/components/mui/` already exists as a folder but is
  still empty — no wrapper components have been written yet, and `src/theme/`
  has no `createTheme()` call wired up either. Don't assume a shared theme
  object exists until `src/theme/index.js` is actually populated.

> Note on PropTypes: `prop-types` is **not** currently listed in
> `package.json` (dependencies or devDependencies) — verify before assuming
> it's installed. The template below shows the intended convention once the
> package is added; if it isn't installed yet when you're doing this task,
> flag that gap rather than silently importing a package that doesn't exist.

### 2. MUI Wrapper Template
```javascript
// src/components/mui/AppButtonComponent.jsx
import React, { memo } from 'react'
import { Button as MuiButton } from '@mui/material'
import PropTypes from 'prop-types'

const AppButtonComponent = ({
  variant = 'contained',
  color = 'primary',
  size = 'medium',
  loading = false,
  disabled = false,
  children,
  onClick,
  sx = {},
  ...props
}) => {
  return (
    <MuiButton
      variant={variant}
      color={color}
      size={size}
      disabled={disabled || loading}
      onClick={onClick}
      sx={{
        textTransform: 'none', // Disable uppercase transformation
        borderRadius: 2,
        fontWeight: 500,
        ...sx
      }}
      {...props}
    >
      {loading ? 'Loading...' : children}
    </MuiButton>
  )
}

AppButtonComponent.propTypes = {
  variant: PropTypes.oneOf(['contained', 'outlined', 'text']),
  color: PropTypes.oneOf(['primary', 'secondary', 'error', 'warning', 'info', 'success']),
  size: PropTypes.oneOf(['small', 'medium', 'large']),
  loading: PropTypes.bool,
  disabled: PropTypes.bool,
  children: PropTypes.node.isRequired,
  onClick: PropTypes.func,
  sx: PropTypes.object
}

export default memo(AppButtonComponent)
```

### 3. Rhynk MUI Wrappers

#### AppTextFieldComponent
```javascript
// src/components/mui/AppTextFieldComponent.jsx
import React, { memo } from 'react'
import { TextField as MuiTextField } from '@mui/material'
import PropTypes from 'prop-types'

const AppTextFieldComponent = ({
  label,
  value,
  onChange,
  error,
  helperText,
  required = false,
  type = 'text',
  placeholder,
  disabled = false,
  sx = {},
  ...props
}) => {
  return (
    <MuiTextField
      label={label}
      value={value}
      onChange={onChange}
      error={!!error}
      helperText={error || helperText}
      required={required}
      type={type}
      placeholder={placeholder}
      disabled={disabled}
      variant="outlined"
      fullWidth
      margin="normal"
      sx={{
        '& .MuiOutlinedInput-root': {
          borderRadius: 2
        },
        ...sx
      }}
      {...props}
    />
  )
}

AppTextFieldComponent.propTypes = {
  label: PropTypes.string,
  value: PropTypes.string.isRequired,
  onChange: PropTypes.func.isRequired,
  error: PropTypes.string,
  helperText: PropTypes.string,
  required: PropTypes.bool,
  type: PropTypes.string,
  placeholder: PropTypes.string,
  disabled: PropTypes.bool,
  sx: PropTypes.object
}

export default memo(AppTextFieldComponent)
```

#### AppCardComponent
```javascript
// src/components/mui/AppCardComponent.jsx
import React, { memo } from 'react'
import { Card as MuiCard, CardContent as MuiCardContent } from '@mui/material'
import PropTypes from 'prop-types'

const AppCardComponent = ({
  children,
  elevation = 1,
  sx = {},
  ...props
}) => {
  return (
    <MuiCard
      elevation={elevation}
      sx={{
        borderRadius: 2,
        transition: 'all 0.2s ease-in-out',
        '&:hover': {
          elevation: 2,
          transform: 'translateY(-2px)'
        },
        ...sx
      }}
      {...props}
    >
      <MuiCardContent>
        {children}
      </MuiCardContent>
    </MuiCard>
  )
}

AppCardComponent.propTypes = {
  children: PropTypes.node.isRequired,
  elevation: PropTypes.number,
  sx: PropTypes.object
}

export default memo(AppCardComponent)
```

#### AppModalComponent
```javascript
// src/components/mui/AppModalComponent.jsx
import React, { memo } from 'react'
import {
  Dialog as MuiDialog,
  DialogTitle as MuiDialogTitle,
  DialogContent as MuiDialogContent,
  DialogActions as MuiDialogActions,
  IconButton
} from '@mui/material'
import { Close as CloseIcon } from '@mui/icons-material'
import PropTypes from 'prop-types'

const AppModalComponent = ({
  open,
  onClose,
  title,
  children,
  actions,
  maxWidth = 'sm',
  fullWidth = true,
  sx = {},
  ...props
}) => {
  return (
    <MuiDialog
      open={open}
      onClose={onClose}
      maxWidth={maxWidth}
      fullWidth={fullWidth}
      sx={{
        '& .MuiDialog-paper': {
          borderRadius: 2
        },
        ...sx
      }}
      {...props}
    >
      {title && (
        <MuiDialogTitle
          sx={{
            display: 'flex',
            justifyContent: 'space-between',
            alignItems: 'center',
            pb: 1
          }}
        >
          {title}
          <IconButton
            onClick={onClose}
            size="small"
            sx={{ ml: 2 }}
          >
            <CloseIcon />
          </IconButton>
        </MuiDialogTitle>
      )}

      <MuiDialogContent>
        {children}
      </MuiDialogContent>

      {actions && (
        <MuiDialogActions>
          {actions}
        </MuiDialogActions>
      )}
    </MuiDialog>
  )
}

AppModalComponent.propTypes = {
  open: PropTypes.bool.isRequired,
  onClose: PropTypes.func.isRequired,
  title: PropTypes.string,
  children: PropTypes.node.isRequired,
  actions: PropTypes.node,
  maxWidth: PropTypes.oneOf(['xs', 'sm', 'md', 'lg', 'xl']),
  fullWidth: PropTypes.bool,
  sx: PropTypes.object
}

export default memo(AppModalComponent)
```

### 4. MUI Wrapper Requirements Checklist

#### ✅ Basic Requirements
- [ ] Create wrapper for every MUI component used
- [ ] Use PropTypes for all prop validation (NO TypeScript) — once `prop-types`
      is installed; confirm it's actually in `package.json` before assuming so
- [ ] Apply consistent styling with SX prop
- [ ] Include proper default props (via default parameters, not
      `Component.defaultProps` — that pattern is deprecated for function
      components in React 19)
- [ ] Use React.memo for performance
- [ ] Follow JSX file structure order

#### ✅ MUI Integration
- [ ] Wrap MUI component with custom props
- [ ] Apply consistent theme integration once `src/theme/index.js` exists
- [ ] Add hover and focus states
- [ ] Ensure accessibility compliance
- [ ] Use MUI's responsive breakpoint system

#### ✅ Rhynk Specific
- [ ] Consider dark-mode-first styling — the PRD's own screenshots skew
      toward a dark, music-app aesthetic; don't assume light-mode-first
      defaults once the theme is built
- [ ] Include proper error/empty states for wrappers used in chat and
      music-room UI (e.g. `AppModalComponent` used for room settings,
      `AppTextFieldComponent` used for the message composer)
- [ ] Add loading states where needed (e.g. a `loading` prop on
      `AppButtonComponent` for send/DJ-action buttons)
- [ ] Consider mobile responsiveness — MUI breakpoints (`xs`/`sm`/`md`), not
      Tailwind prefixes
- [ ] Add proper data validation for props coming from RTK Query responses

